-- title:
--   Original bounded-variation Lévy sample-dependent stopped physical Taylor positive error vanishes in L1
-- statement:
--   For the actual BV SpectrallyNegativeLevy process X and original admissible dividend strategy D on a deterministic physical mesh with measurable, sample-dependent bounded stopped index k, the exact discounted original C1 Taylor source error has integrable positive part at each n and expected positive part tending to zero. The proof uses original measurable stochastic evaluations and the real masked stopped prefix, then the already Proved variable-endpoint BV variation DCT theorem. Genuine compact C1 band and fine-mesh events are explicitly assumed; no signed BV prebudget or stochastic estimate is imported.
-- source:
--   Composed proof of original stopped-grid positive error convergence from Proved P3-F2 type, original mask and exact stopped-grid prefix identity.

